From 1d48ead5fc06de8ea082e201b3c87914e4e2d7ba Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Brandon Williams <turbine.bmw@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 14 Oct 2026 00:16:47 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 2335/2368] media: qcom: camss: x1e80100: white balance, gamma
 and black level on the PIX line

The front-end modules of the IFE gate their clocks while disabled and
drop register writes, so set the top clock gating overrides (the GPL
Titan driver's core_cgc_ovd_0/1 and ahb_cgc_ovd) before programming.

Then enable white balance at unity gain (Q10 gains for G, B and R in
bits 31:17 of +0x68, +0x6c and +0x70, as in the OPE; the register at
+0x94 resets to a value that leaves green wrong and takes all ones),
load a gamma 2.2 table for all three channels through the GLUT's DMI
port (256 entries of 12-bit output values, the OPE's load sequence), and
subtract the sensor black level on the colour transform input through
the new pix_black_level module parameter. The chroma coefficients sum
to zero, so the offset only moves luma.

The TPG colour bars still read their BT.601 values, and the ramp now
follows the gamma curve.

Signed-off-by: Brandon Williams <turbine.bmw@gmail.com>
(cherry picked from commit 67bd3b468c491ae4b15af52da7255363b8417f9b)

